From: danyi <308664957+mydanyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wsa884x: preserve compander gain on Pocket S2

Pocket S2 uses matched WSA macro and amplifier companders with digital
volume control. The amplifier POST_PMU sequence selects the compander,
but unmute immediately overrides it with the fixed CSR gain. Retain the
compander selection when its port is enabled on this board.

The matching UCM must enable both macro companders, initialize both PA
controls to 17 (hardware gain index 14, unity), and use digital volume.
Limit this change to Pocket S2; existing configurations on other WSA884x
machines continue to use the original fixed-gain behavior.

Signed-off-by: danyi <308664957+mydanyi@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
 #include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
 #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>
@@ -1804,6 +1805,7 @@
 static int wsa884x_mute_stream(struct snd_soc_dai *dai, int mute, int stream)
 {
 	struct snd_soc_component *component = dai->component;
+	struct wsa884x_priv *wsa884x = snd_soc_component_get_drvdata(component);
 
 	if (mute) {
 		snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1,
@@ -1814,9 +1816,11 @@
 					      0x0);
 
 	} else {
+		/* Pocket S2 uses digital volume with matched SoundWire companders. */
 		snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1,
 					      WSA884X_DRE_CTL_1_CSR_GAIN_EN_MASK,
-					      0x1);
+					      !of_machine_is_compatible("ayaneo,pocket-s2") ||
+					      !wsa884x->port_enable[WSA884X_PORT_COMP]);
 		snd_soc_component_write_field(component, WSA884X_PA_FSM_EN,
 					      WSA884X_PA_FSM_EN_GLOBAL_PA_EN_MASK,
 					      0x1);
